import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(1,1,"What Is the Mind? A First Look","Choose one strong reaction this week. On paper, write the bare facts on one side, as a camera would, and on the other what you brought. Where did the situation end and where did you begin?",[
mc("U","When Swamiji asks the group “What is the mind?”, what does he point out about their answers?",
 ["Each trails off after a few sentences, although we use the mind every moment of our lives.","Each gives a different correct answer, which shows how rich the subject is for everyone.","Each answer is wrong, which shows that none of the three has ever thought about the mind.","Each answer agrees with the others, which shows that the mind is easy to define in words."],0,
 "Three thoughtful people became uncertain within a few sentences. We use the mind from waking to sleeping, yet when asked what it is we can barely speak. Swamiji calls this gap consequential, not embarrassing: education makes us literate about the body but gives us almost no comparable literacy about the mind, which is the reason for this course.",
 "We use the mind every moment yet cannot say what it is","Part 1"),
mc("U","What does Swamiji say is missing, despite the many talks, books and apps about the mind?",
 ["A working model: a coherent map of the mind's structure and functions, like anatomy.","More information, since there are still too few books and apps for people to learn from.","More belief, since people need to trust one authority before any study of the mind can start.","More brain scans, since only measurement can show what the mind really is and how it acts."],0,
 "There is no shortage of information; searching gives many conflicting answers. What is missing is a working model of the mind: a coherent map of its structure and its functions, in the way that anatomy gives us a map of the body.",
 "What is missing is a working model of the mind","Part 1"),
mc("A","Kai reads a short message as dismissive and is wound up for hours. Next morning the same words seem neutral. What does the lesson say about this?",
 ["The words stayed the same; what he brought to them changed, so the experience was X meeting his state, Y.","The words changed overnight, so the friend must have sent a second and gentler message.","His morning self was mistaken, so the evening reading was the true one and should be kept.","His mood did not matter at all, so the difference must have come from the friend alone."],0,
 "Swamiji says the spiral was the meeting of the message and Kai’s state. Both were real, but together they felt more alarming than either alone.",
 "Same words, different Y","Part 3"),
mc("A","James teaches the same lesson to two classes: one debates, the other is flat. Which idea does he use to understand it?",
 ["The lesson was the same but the students were not: each child brings a different Y into the room.","The lesson must have been delivered differently, so he should look for his own error first.","The flat class is less able, so he should simplify the lesson for it and move on at once.","The debating class is the typical one, so the flat class must have something wrong with it."],0,
 "It is the Y each child carries in: history with the subject, history with adults, what happened before they sat down. Swamiji adds that a teacher should try to understand something about the Y in the room.",
 "The Y in the room differs, so the same lesson lands differently","Part 3"),
judge("“Thought is a map of experience: useful and sometimes indispensable, but the map is not the land.”",T,
 "Thought always arrives after experience: you hear a sound and then identify it, meet someone and then form an opinion. Thought is the mind catching up with what has already happened, and it is valuable, since without it there would be no science, language or deep relationship.",
 "Thought is a map, not the land","Part 2"),
mc("U","Why can a feeling of danger persist when there is no real danger, according to the lesson?",
 ["A fast threat-detection system, the amygdala, can fire before the thinking brain has assessed the situation.","The thinking brain always fires first, so the feeling is only a mistake of reasoning.","The body has no alarm system, so a feeling of danger is always a sign of real danger nearby.","Fear is a habit of the culture, so it disappears when a person stops talking about danger."],0,
 "The alarm system evolved to keep us alive, not to be accurate in every situation. It responds to patterns from the past, not necessarily to what is fully present now, which is why James’s students can feel danger in a safe classroom.",
 "The alarm can fire before thinking has assessed","Part 2"),
judge("“If a person is sincere in a moral judgement, it follows that the judgement is complete and correct.”",F,
 "Conscience, responsibility and honesty are essential, but what you take to be right is shaped by upbringing, culture, history, fears and hopes. You can be sincere and still be missing something: the judgement may be good and still be partial.",
 "Sincerity does not guarantee accuracy","Part 2"),
mc("A","Sarah notices a running commentary in her head while she is with her daughter: “she’s doing this wrong, I should have said that differently.” What does she realise?",
 ["That she has stopped actually being with her daughter, since the commentary has taken the place of the experience.","That the commentary shows she is a very good mother, since she is thinking about her child all the time.","That the commentary is useless, so she should stop all thought whenever she is with another person.","That the commentary is the daughter’s fault, since it begins only when the daughter speaks."],0,
 "Thought is the mind’s commentary on an experience, not the experience. When commentary runs, we can stop being with the person. Swamiji calls this a precise observation.",
 "Commentary can replace actually being there","Part 2"),
mc("A","A worried parent looks at a closed bedroom door and hears danger; a more settled parent hears nothing. Which statement fits the lesson?",
 ["The door is the same and the Y is different, so the experience is X meeting what each parent brings.","The door is different in the two homes, so the two parents are simply reacting to different facts.","The settled parent is cold, so she cannot be reading the situation as accurately as the worried one.","The worried parent is simply wrong, so she should take the settled parent’s view and say no more."],0,
 "Swamiji presents this as the structure of all human knowing, not a criticism. The door (X) is the same; the Y, the history, mood and predictions each brings, is different.",
 "Same door, different Y","Part 3"),
mc("A","For the practical experiment, what should a person write down on the “X” side of the paper?",
 ["Only the bare facts, what was said or done, as if a camera were recording it, with no interpretation.","Their opinion of the other person, so that they can see clearly whether it was justified.","Their mood and their history with the person, since these are what really caused the reaction.","Their plan for what to say next time, so that the same reaction does not happen again."],0,
 "The Y side holds what you brought: mood, history with this person, what you feared or hoped, what the moment reminded you of. Then ask: where did the situation end and where did I begin? No judging or changing yet, just seeing.",
 "X is the camera record: the bare facts","Practical situation")])
